phase I, 2 charges

round I.1
dealer gets phone
dealer loads 2 live, 1 blank
player shoots dealer, live

!check shells = 1 live, 1 blank

dealer uses phone
!check theories
!check known shells
!check theories = 2
# he could have seen:
#   - next one blank (so knows that this one is live)
#   - next one live (so knows that this one is blank)

dealer shoots player, live
!check theories = 1
# - suppose he had learned before that the next turn's shell was blank, then
#   he would be able to reason that this shell is live, and would decide to
#   shoot us. as this is consistent with what he did, so we can't eliminate
#   theory.
# - suppose he had learned before that the next turn's shell was live, then
#   he would be able to reason that this shell is blank, and would shoot himself
#   to get another turn. this contradicts what he did, so we must eliminate this
#   theory.

# because, in all the remaining theories, the dealer knows that the next shell is blank, then:
# - we know that he knows that the next shell is blank
# - we know the next shell is blank
!check theories
!check known shells
